{"case": "own-wl-069", "search_mode": "unavailable", "sources": ["web_tool.py curl 2026-11-06T13:46:53.857224+00:00"], "complete": true, "pages": [{"url": "https://www.iana.org/assignments/service-names-port-numbers/service-names-port-numbers.xhtml?search=tftp", "finalUrl": "https://www.iana.org/assignments/service-names-port-numbers?search=tftp", "at": "2026-11-06T13:46:53.857224+00:00", "status": 200, "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "bytes": 37989, "body": "\n<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<head>\n\t<title>Service Name and Transport Protocol Port Number Registry</title>\n\n\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n\t<meta http-equiv=\"Content-type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\" />\n\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n\t\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/static/css/iana_website.68dd615b61e5.css\"/>\n    <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" type=\"image/ico\" href=\"/static/img/bookmark_icon.e14a2530b3e9.ico\"/>\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/static/js/jquery.a8e7cabd4d49.js\"></script>\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/static/js/dtable.46ee921d4414.js\" defer></script>\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/static/js/relative-time.afe302b05f0d.js\" defer></script>\n\n\t\n</head>\n\n<body>\n\n\n\n<header class=\"full-width\">\n    <div id=\"header\">\n        <div id=\"logo\">\n            <a href=\"/\"><img src=\"/static/img/iana-logo-header.426b3ac01d35.svg\" alt=\"Homepage\"/></a>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"navigation\">\n            <ul>\n                <li><a href=\"/domains\">Domains</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"/protocols\">Protocols</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"/numbers\">Numbers</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"/about\">About</a></li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    \n</header>\n\n<div id=\"body\">\n<article class=\"hemmed sidenav full-width\">\n    <main>\n<div class=\"registry-content\">\n<div class=\"registry\" id=\"service-names-port-numbers\"><h1>Service Name and Transport Protocol Port Number Registry</h1>\n<h3 class=\"registry-meta\">Last Updated</h3><ul class=\"registry-refs\"><li>2026-11-05</li></ul><h3 class=\"registry-meta\">Expert(s)</h3><ul class=\"registry-refs\"><li>TCP/UDP: Joe Touch; Eliot Lear, Kumiko Ono, Wes Eddy, Brian Trammell, and Michael Scharf</li><li>SCTP: Michael Tuexen</li><li>DCCP: Eddie Kohler and Yoshifumi Nishida</li></ul><h3 class=\"registry-meta\">Reference</h3><ul class=\"registry-refs\"><li><a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc6335\">RFC 6335</a>: Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) Procedures for the Management of the Service Name and Transport Protocol Port Number Registry</li></ul><h3 class=\"registry-meta\">Note</h3><p>Service names and port numbers are used to distinguish between different services that run\nover transport protocols such as TCP, UDP, DCCP, and SCTP.</p>\n<p>Service names are assigned on a First Come First Served basis, as described in <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc6335\">RFC 6335</a>.</p>\n<p>Port numbers are divided into three ranges, with their uses and assignment procedures specified in <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc6335#section-8.1.2\">Section 8.1.2 of RFC 6335</a>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>System Ports (0-1023) are assigned using the <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc8126#section-4.8\">IETF Review</a> or <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc8126#section-4.10\">IESG Approval</a> procedures.</li>\n<li>User Ports (1024-49151) are assigned using the <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc8126#section-4.8\">IETF Review</a>, <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc8126#section-4.10\">IESG Approval</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc8126#section-4.5\">Expert Review</a> procedures.</li>\n<li>Dynamic and/or Private Ports (49152-65535) are not assigned.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The registration procedures for service names and port numbers are specified in <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc6335\">RFC 6335</a>, while the registration policies referenced above are defined in <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/go/rfc8126\">RFC 8126</a>.</p>\n<p>Assigned ports both System and User ports SHOULD NOT be used without or prior to IANA registration.</p><div class=\"panel_warning icon\"><p>Assignment of a port number does not in any way imply an\nendorsement of an application or product, and the fact that network\ntraffic is flowing to or from a registered port does not mean that\nit is \"good\" traffic, nor that it necessarily corresponds to the\nassigned service. Firewall and system administrators should\nchoose how to configure their systems based on their knowledge of\nthe traffic in question, not whether there is a port number\nregistered or not.</p></div><h3 class=\"registry-meta\">Registration Forms</h3><ul>\n<li>To request a new assignment, please use the <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/form/ports-services\">Application for Service Names and User Port Numbers</a> form.</li>\n<li>To modify an existing assignment, please use the <a href=\"https://www.iana.org/form/port-modification\">Modify a Port Number Assignment</a> form.</li>\n</ul><h3 class=\"registry-meta\">Available Formats</h3><ul class=\"registry-refs registry-formats\"><li><a href=\"/assignments/service-names-port-numbers/service-names-port-numbers.csv\">CSV</a></li><li><a href=\"/assignments/service-names-port-numbers/service-names-port-numbers.xml\">XML</a></li><li><a href=\"/assignments/service-names-port-numbers\">HTML</a></li><li><a href=\"/assignments/service-names-port-numbers/service-names-port-numbers.txt\">TXT</a></li></ul>\n<form action=\"?search=tftp\" method=\"get\">\n<input name=\"search\" size=\"18\" type=\"text\" value=\"tftp\"/>\n<input type=\"submit\" value=\"Search\"/>\n</form>\n<div class=\"dtable-wrap dtable-wrap--shade\"><table class=\"sortable_srv dtable dtable--divided dtable--compact\" id=\"table-service-names-port-numbers\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Service <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Name<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"sortNumeric dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Port <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Number<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Transport <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Protocol<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\"><span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Description<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\"><span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Assignee<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\"><span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Contact<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Registration <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Date<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Modification <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Date<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\"><span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Reference<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Service <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Code<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Unauthorized Use <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Reported<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Assignment <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Notes<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>tftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">69</td>\n<td align=\"center\">tcp</td>\n<td>Trivial File Transfer</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"David_Clark\" href=\"#David_Clark\">David Clark</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"David_Clark\" href=\"#David_Clark\">David Clark</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>tftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">69</td>\n<td align=\"center\">udp</td>\n<td>Trivial File Transfer</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"David_Clark\" href=\"#David_Clark\">David Clark</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"David_Clark\" href=\"#David_Clark\">David Clark</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>subntbcst-tftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">247</td>\n<td align=\"center\">tcp</td>\n<td>SUBNTBCST_TFTP<br/><br/>\nIANA assigned this well-formed service name as a replacement for \"subntbcst_tftp\".</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>subntbcst_tftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">247</td>\n<td align=\"center\">tcp</td>\n<td>SUBNTBCST_TFTP</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>This entry is an alias to \"subntbcst-tftp\".\nThis entry is now historic, not usable for use with many\ncommon service discovery mechanisms.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>subntbcst-tftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">247</td>\n<td align=\"center\">udp</td>\n<td>SUBNTBCST_TFTP<br/><br/>\nIANA assigned this well-formed service name as a replacement for \"subntbcst_tftp\".</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>subntbcst_tftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">247</td>\n<td align=\"center\">udp</td>\n<td>SUBNTBCST_TFTP</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"John_Fake\" href=\"#John_Fake\">John Fake</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>This entry is an alias to \"subntbcst-tftp\".\nThis entry is now historic, not usable for use with many\ncommon service discovery mechanisms.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>tftp-mcast</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1758</td>\n<td align=\"center\">tcp</td>\n<td>tftp-mcast</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Tom_Emberson\" href=\"#Tom_Emberson\">Tom Emberson</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Tom_Emberson\" href=\"#Tom_Emberson\">Tom Emberson</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>tftp-mcast</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1758</td>\n<td align=\"center\">udp</td>\n<td>tftp-mcast</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Tom_Emberson\" href=\"#Tom_Emberson\">Tom Emberson</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Tom_Emberson\" href=\"#Tom_Emberson\">Tom Emberson</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>etftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1818</td>\n<td align=\"center\">tcp</td>\n<td>Enhanced Trivial File Transfer Protocol</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"William_Polites\" href=\"#William_Polites\">William Polites</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"William_Polites\" href=\"#William_Polites\">William Polites</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>etftp</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1818</td>\n<td align=\"center\">udp</td>\n<td>Enhanced Trivial File Transfer Protocol</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"William_Polites\" href=\"#William_Polites\">William Polites</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"William_Polites\" href=\"#William_Polites\">William Polites</a></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>tftps</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3713</td>\n<td align=\"center\">tcp</td>\n<td>TFTP over TLS</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Mark_mayernick\" href=\"#Mark_mayernick\">Mark mayernick</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Mark_mayernick\" href=\"#Mark_mayernick\">Mark mayernick</a></td>\n<td>2003-03</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>tftps</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3713</td>\n<td align=\"center\">udp</td>\n<td>TFTP over TLS</td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Mark_mayernick\" href=\"#Mark_mayernick\">Mark mayernick</a></td>\n<td><a data-contact=\"Mark_mayernick\" href=\"#Mark_mayernick\">Mark mayernick</a></td>\n<td>2003-03</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n</div><hr/><h2 class=\"people\">Contact Information</h2>\n<div class=\"dtable-wrap dtable-wrap--shade\"><table class=\"sortable dtable dtable--divided dtable--compact\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\"><span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Name<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Contact <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">URI<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n<th aria-sort=\"none\" class=\"dtable-sortable\" tabindex=\"0\">Last <span class=\"dtable-sort-tail\">Updated<span class=\"dtable-sort\"></span></span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr id=\"David_Clark\">\n\n<td>David Clark</td>\n<td><a href=\"mailto:ddc&amp;lcs.mit.edu\">ddc&amp;lcs.mit.edu</a></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr id=\"John_Fake\">\n\n<td>John Fake</td>\n<td><a href=\"mailto:fake&amp;us.ibm.com\">fake&amp;us.ibm.com</a></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr id=\"Mark_mayernick\">\n\n<td>Mark mayernick</td>\n<td><a href=\"mailto:Mark.Mayernick&amp;thomson.net\">Mark.Mayernick&amp;thomson.net</a></td>\n<td>2003-03</td>\n</tr>\n<tr id=\"Tom_Emberson\">\n\n<td>Tom Emberson</td>\n<td><a href=\"mailto:tom&amp;lanworks.com\">tom&amp;lanworks.com</a></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr id=\"William_Polites\">\n\n<td>William Polites</td>\n<td><a href=\"mailto:wpolites&amp;mitre.org\">wpolites&amp;mitre.org</a></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n</div>\n</main>\n    \n\n\n</article>\n</div>\n<footer class=\"full-width\">\n    <div id=\"footer\">\n        <table class=\"navigation\">\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"section\"><a href=\"/domains\">Domain&nbsp;Names</a></td>\n                <td class=\"subsection\">\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/domains/root\">Root Zone Registry</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/domains/int\">.INT Registry</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/domains/arpa\">.ARPA Registry</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/domains/idn-tables\">IDN Repository</a></li>\n                    </ul>\n                </td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"section\"><a href=\"/numbers\">Number&nbsp;Resources</a></td>\n                <td class=\"subsection\">\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/numbers/registries\">Number Registries</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/numbers/allocations/\">RIR Allocation Data</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/help/abuse\">Abuse Information</a></li>\n                    </ul>\n                </td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"section\"><a href=\"/protocols\">Protocols</a></td>\n                <td class=\"subsection\">\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/protocols\">Protocol Registries</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/time-zones\">Time Zone Database</a></li>\n                    </ul>\n                </td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td class=\"section\"><a href=\"/about\">About&nbsp;Us</a></td>\n                <td class=\"subsection\">\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/news\">News</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/performance\">Performance</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/about/organization\">The Organization</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/archive\">Archive</a></li>\n                        <li><a href=\"/contact\">Contact Us</a></li>\n                    </ul>\n                </td>\n            </tr>\n        </table>\n        <div id=\"custodian\">\n            <p>The IANA functions coordinate the Internet’s globally unique identifiers, and\n                are provided by <a href=\"https://pti.icann.org\">Public Technical Identifiers</a>, an affiliate of\n                <a href=\"https://www.icann.org/\">ICANN</a>.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"legalnotice\">\n            <ul>\n                <li><a href=\"https://www.icann.org/privacy/policy\">Privacy Policy</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"https://www.icann.org/privacy/tos\">Terms of Service</a></li>\n                \n                <li><a href=\"/help/licensing-terms\">Licensing Terms</a></li>\n                \n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</footer>\n\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n// Registry side nav: hierarchy, filtering, and scroll tracking.\n(function () {\n    \"use strict\";\n\n    var nav = document.querySelector(\".registry-nav\");\n    if (!nav) return;\n\n    // Distance below the viewport top at which a section counts as current.\n    var SCROLLSPY_LINE = 120;\n\n    var items = Array.prototype.slice.call(nav.querySelectorAll(\".registry-nav-item\"));\n    var toggles = Array.prototype.slice.call(nav.querySelectorAll(\".registry-nav-toggle\"));\n    var filter = nav.querySelector(\"#registry-nav-filter\");\n    var status = nav.querySelector(\".registry-nav-status\");\n    var clearFilter = nav.querySelector(\".dtable-search__clear\");\n\n    function setExpanded(item, expanded) {\n        var toggle = item.querySelector(\":scope > .registry-nav-toggle\");\n        if (!toggle) return;\n        item.classList.toggle(\"is-collapsed\", !expanded);\n        toggle.setAttribute(\"aria-expanded\", expanded ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n        var title = item.querySelector(\":scope > a\");\n        toggle.setAttribute(\n            \"aria-label\",\n            (expanded ? \"Collapse \" : \"Expand \") + (title ? title.getAttribute(\"data-title\") : \"\")\n        );\n    }\n\n    function ancestors(el) {\n        var out = [];\n        for (var p = el.parentElement; p && nav.contains(p); p = p.parentElement) {\n            if (p.classList.contains(\"registry-nav-item\")) out.push(p);\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    function revealItem(item) {\n        ancestors(item).forEach(function (parent) {\n            setExpanded(parent, true);\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Branches start expanded; just wire up the toggles.\n\n    toggles.forEach(function (toggle) {\n        toggle.addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n            var item = toggle.closest(\".registry-nav-item\");\n            setExpanded(item, item.classList.contains(\"is-collapsed\"));\n        });\n    });\n\n    // ===== Phone and tablet drawer =====\n    // The checkbox in the template already opens/closes the off-canvas nav\n    // via CSS alone (see _apps.scss), so it works with no JavaScript\n    // at all. This just layers on convenience: closing after a tap, Escape,\n    // a resize past the breakpoint, and locking body scroll while it's open.\n\n    // The element an in-page link points at. A fragment that isn't valid\n    // percent-encoding (a stray \"%\") is looked up as written.\n    function fragmentTarget(href) {\n        if (!href || href.charAt(0) !== \"#\") return null;\n        var id = href.slice(1);\n        try {\n            id = decodeURIComponent(id);\n        } catch (e) {}\n        return document.getElementById(id);\n    }\n\n    var mobileCheckbox = document.getElementById(\"registry-nav-checkbox\");\n    var NAV_DRAWER_QUERY = \"(max-width: 1000px)\"; // $breakpoint-lg in _apps.scss\n\n    // Closing the drawer hides it (visibility: hidden), which would strand\n    // focus inside it, so hand focus back to the toggle (its :focus-visible\n    // ring shows on the label). Not past the breakpoint: there the nav is a\n    // visible sidebar and focus can stay where it is. Not after following a\n    // link either (keepFocus): focus goes to the chosen section instead.\n    // Focus that is elsewhere on the page stays put; focus that is on nothing\n    // (the body) goes to the toggle too.\n    function setNavOpen(open, keepFocus) {\n        var active = document.activeElement;\n        var strandFocus = !open && !keepFocus && mobileCheckbox && mobileCheckbox.checked &&\n            (!active || active === document.body || nav.contains(active)) &&\n            window.matchMedia(NAV_DRAWER_QUERY).matches;\n        if (mobileCheckbox) mobileCheckbox.checked = open;\n        document.body.classList.toggle(\"registry-nav-open\", open);\n        if (strandFocus) mobileCheckbox.focus({preventScroll: true});\n    }\n\n    if (mobileCheckbox) {\n        mobileCheckbox.addEventListener(\"change\", function () {\n            document.body.classList.toggle(\"registry-nav-open\", mobileCheckbox.checked);\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Closing after a tap lets the user actually see the section they picked.\n    // Focus moves to that section too: left on the link, it would be stranded\n    // in the hidden drawer, and a section that isn't focusable doesn't take\n    // focus from the fragment navigation by itself. preventScroll leaves the\n    // scrolling to the link's own navigation. A section made focusable only\n    // for this loses its tabindex again once focus moves on. Modified clicks\n    // (open in a new tab) navigate elsewhere, so the drawer stays as it is.\n    // A link to a section that doesn't exist hands focus back to the toggle.\n    nav.addEventListener(\"click\", function (event) {\n        var link = event.target.closest(\"a\");\n        if (!link || !window.matchMedia(NAV_DRAWER_QUERY).matches) return;\n        if (event.defaultPrevented || event.button !== 0 ||\n            event.ctrlKey || event.metaKey || event.shiftKey || event.altKey) return;\n        var section = fragmentTarget(link.getAttribute(\"href\"));\n        setNavOpen(false, !!section);\n        if (section) {\n            if (!section.hasAttribute(\"tabindex\")) {\n                section.setAttribute(\"tabindex\", \"-1\");\n                section.classList.add(\"registry-nav-target\");\n                section.addEventListener(\"blur\", function () {\n                    section.removeAttribute(\"tabindex\");\n                    section.classList.remove(\"registry-nav-target\");\n                }, {once: true});\n            }\n            section.focus({preventScroll: true});\n        }\n    });\n\n    window.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (event) {\n        if (event.key === \"Escape\" && mobileCheckbox && mobileCheckbox.checked) setNavOpen(false);\n    });\n\n    // A resize past the breakpoint (e.g. rotating the device) shouldn't\n    // leave the drawer open with no toggle left to close it.\n    window.addEventListener(\"resize\", function () {\n        if (!window.matchMedia(NAV_DRAWER_QUERY).matches) setNavOpen(false);\n    });\n\n    // ===== Filtering =====\n\n    // Search only visible label text; the screen-reader-only elided prefix is excluded\n    function labelNode(link) {\n        var label = link.querySelector(\".registry-nav-label\");\n        if (!label) return null;\n        return Array.prototype.find.call(label.childNodes, function (node) {\n            return node.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE && node.nodeValue.trim() !== \"\";\n        });\n    }\n\n    function markMatch(link, term) {\n        var node = labelNode(link);